.TH READLINK 1 "5th of August 2026" "zenithutils" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
readlink - ask symbolic links where they point to

.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBreadlink\fP [-fevqn] file [...]

.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBreadlink\fP takes one or more paths as arguments, and gives where they point to as symlinks

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB-f\fP
canonicalize paths

.TP
\fB-e\fP
canonicalize paths and ensure it exists

.TP
\fB-v\fP
verbose mode, print error messages

.TP
\fB-q\fP
quiet mode, read link but do not print filename (exit code only)

.TP
\fB-n\fP
no newline after filename (only applies if there's one argument)

.SH SEE ALSO
readlink(2)
